msgid "Apply Firewall Settings"
msgstr ""

msgid "Creates the \"tailscale\" interface and firewall zone if needed, then allows exactly the traffic you tick below. Nothing is allowed that is not ticked. These settings are applied immediately and independently of \"Save & Apply\"."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tailscale"
msgstr ""

msgid "Tailscale is a mesh VPN that connects your devices securely. Everything is off until you enable the service below."
msgstr ""

msgid "General"
msgstr ""

msgid "Account"
msgstr ""

msgid "Firewall"
msgstr ""

msgid "Devices"
msgstr ""

msgid "Advanced"
msgstr ""

msgid "Enable Tailscale"
msgstr ""

msgid "Turns the Tailscale service on or off. When off, the daemon is stopped and does not start at boot."
msgstr ""

msgid "Name of this device in your tailnet. Leave empty to use the system hostname."
msgstr ""

msgid "Accept Routes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Accept subnet routes advertised by other devices in your tailnet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Advertise Routes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Subnets behind this router that other tailnet devices may reach (subnet router). Pick a detected subnet or enter your own in CIDR notation. The routes still have to be approved in the Tailscale admin console."
msgstr ""

msgid "Advertise Exit Node"
msgstr ""

msgid "Offer this device as an exit node for internet traffic. Ignored while an exit node is selected below. Allow \"Tailnet devices may access the internet\" in the Firewall tab."
msgstr ""

msgid "Use Exit Node"
msgstr ""

msgid "Route this router's internet traffic through another device. For LAN clients to use it, allow \"LAN devices may access the tailnet\" in the Firewall tab. If you pick a device here, \"Advertise Exit Node\" is switched off."
msgstr ""

msgid "None"
msgstr ""

msgid "not in the current device list"
msgstr ""

msgid "Allow LAN Access"
msgstr ""

msgid "While using an exit node, keep direct access to the local network. Recommended on a router, otherwise LAN traffic is sent through the exit node."
msgstr ""

msgid "Tailscale SSH"
msgstr ""

msgid "Let Tailscale run an SSH server for this device, with access controlled by your tailnet policy."
msgstr ""

msgid "Shields Up"
msgstr ""

msgid "Block all incoming connections from the tailnet."
msgstr ""

msgid "Web Interface"
msgstr ""

msgid "Expose the Tailscale web interface on port 5252, reachable over the tailnet only."
msgstr ""

msgid "Disable SNAT for Subnet Routes"
msgstr ""

msgid "Keep the original source address for traffic to advertised subnets. Most users should leave this off. It also breaks exit node traffic."
msgstr ""

msgid "Stateful Filtering"
msgstr ""

msgid "Only forward reply traffic for subnet routers and exit nodes. Extra protection for forwarded packets."
msgstr ""

msgid "DNS Mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "Disabled: system DNS only."
msgstr ""

msgid "MagicDNS: Tailscale manages DNS settings of this device."
msgstr ""

msgid "OpenWrt Forward: dnsmasq forwards ts.net names to Tailscale (ts.net only)."
msgstr ""

msgid "OpenWrt Forward"
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer Relay"
msgstr ""

msgid "Act as a Peer Relay server for other devices. Needs a public IP address and an open UDP port."
msgstr ""

msgid "Peer Relay Port"
msgstr ""

msgid "UDP port of the Peer Relay. Open it in your firewall and NAT."
msgstr ""

msgid "Custom Login Server"
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional: URL of a custom control server such as Headscale, for example %s. Leave empty for the default Tailscale service."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enter a valid http:// or https:// URL."
msgstr ""

msgid "Auth Key"
msgstr ""

msgid "Optional: log in with an auth key instead of the browser. The key is used once and is not saved anywhere."
msgstr ""

msgid "Login"
msgstr ""

msgid "Logs this device in. With an auth key it logs in directly, otherwise a login page opens in a new tab."
msgstr ""

msgid "Log in"
msgstr ""

msgid "Disconnects this device from the tailnet and expires its node key."
msgstr ""

msgid "Log out"
msgstr ""

msgid "Firewall Backend"
msgstr ""

msgid "Firewall backend used by the Tailscale daemon. Applying a change restarts the daemon."
msgstr ""

msgid "Listen Port"
msgstr ""

msgid "UDP port of the daemon (default 41641). Useful when you forward a port for direct connections. Applying a change restarts the daemon."
msgstr ""

msgid "State File"
msgstr ""

msgid "Where the daemon keeps its identity. A different path creates a new device and requires a new login. Never use a path in /tmp or /var, it is lost on reboot. Applying a change restarts the daemon."
msgstr ""

msgid "Enter an absolute path without spaces."
msgstr ""

msgid "Log Standard Output"
msgstr ""

msgid "Send the daemon's regular messages to the system log."
msgstr ""

msgid "Log Errors"
msgstr ""

msgid "Send the daemon's error messages to the system log."
msgstr ""

